      "cwe_id": "CWE-89",
      "explanation": "The user-controlled input `q` from `request.args.get` is directly interpolated into a SQL query string using an f-string and executed via `session.execute(text(sql))`. This allows an attacker to inject arbitrary SQL commands (e.g., `q = \"' OR 1=1 --\"`).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "file": "app/routes/orders.py",
          "lines": [
            63,
            69
          ],
          "source": null,
          "content": "    q = request.args.get(\"q\", \"\")\n    session = get_session()\n    sql = (\n        f\"SELECT id, user_id, status, total FROM orders \"\n        f\"WHERE user_id = {g.current_user.id} AND shipping_address LIKE '%{q}%'\"\n    )\n    rows = session.execute(text(sql))",
          "snapshot": null,
          "snapshot_conflict": false,
          "grounded_in_pr": true
        }
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Use parameterized queries. Replace the f-string with a query using bound parameters, e.g., `sql = text(\"SELECT id, user_id, status, total FROM orders WHERE user_id = :user_id AND shipping_address LIKE :q\")` and execute with `session.execute(sql, {\"user_id\": g.current_user.id, \"q\": f\"%{q}%\"})`.",
